        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed all three issues in `collapsible.tsx`, but I couldn't re-run the linter to confirm: running Biome needed approval, and this run is non-interactive.\n\n**The fix:** the clickable header was a plain `<div>` with only a click handler (`collapsible.tsx:122`). I changed it to a `<button type=\"button\">`. A button is interactive and works from the keyboard on its own: it can be focused with Tab, and Enter or Space call the same `openTrigger`. That clears all three rules without adding key handlers. I didn't use `role=\"button\"` plus `tabIndex` plus `onKeyDown` because Ultracite would probably flag that and suggest a real `<button>` instead.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- **`aria-expanded={open}`:** screen readers now announce whether the section is open or closed.\n- **Style reset:** added `background: none`, `border: none`, `padding: 0`, `font`/`color: inherit`, `textAlign: inherit` and `width: 100%`. Without these, the browser's default button styling would change how the header looks; with them it should match the old `<div>`.\n\n**Two things to check:**\n- **Heading inside the button:** Excalidraw passes an `<h3>` as `label`. HTML doesn't allow headings inside a `<button>`. Browsers display it fine, but screen readers won't treat it as a heading any more. The fully correct pattern is `<h3><button aria-expanded>…</button></h3>`. That means changing the caller (`Stats/index.tsx`) or the `label` prop, and both are outside this file.\n- **Caller styles:** inline styles take priority over class styles. If the `className` passed in sets `padding`, `background`, `border` or `width`, the reset will now override it, so it's worth a look at those callers.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "**Other changes:** - **`aria-expanded={open}`:** screen readers now announce whether the section is open or closed. - **Style reset:** added `background: none`, `border: none`, `padding: 0`, `font`/`color: inherit`, `textAlign: inherit` and `width: 100%`.",
          "Without these, the browser's default button styling would change how the header looks; with them it should match the old `<div>`.",
          "That means changing the caller (`Stats/index.tsx`) or the `label` prop, and both are outside this file. - **Caller styles:** inline styles take priority over class styles.",
          "If the `className` passed in sets `padding`, `background`, `border` or `width`, the reset will now override it, so it's worth a look at those callers."
